Q: How to convert Excel to XML with nested elements using XSLT 1.0? A: <p>Transforming one dimension markup to hierarchy is a grouping problem. In this case a <code>group-starting-with</code> problem.</p>

<p>In XSLT 2.0 </p>

<pre><code>&lt;xsl:stylesheet xmlns:xsl="http://www.w3.org/1999/XSL/Transform" version="2.0"&gt;
    &lt;xsl:template match="Table"&gt;
        &lt;xsl:for-each-group 
            select="Row[.//Data]" 
            group-starting-with="Row[count(.//Data)=1]"&gt;
            &lt;Categorie&gt;
                &lt;xsl:for-each-group 
                    select="current-group()[position()&gt;1]" 
                    group-starting-with="Row[count(.//Data)=2]"&gt;
                    &lt;xsl:choose&gt;
                        &lt;xsl:when test="not(self::Row[count(.//Data)=2])"&gt;
                            &lt;xsl:apply-templates select="current-group()"/&gt;
                        &lt;/xsl:when&gt;
                        &lt;xsl:otherwise&gt;
                            &lt;Region&gt;
                                &lt;xsl:apply-templates 
                                    select="current-group()[position()&gt;1]"/&gt;
                            &lt;/Region&gt;
                        &lt;/xsl:otherwise&gt;
                    &lt;/xsl:choose&gt;
                &lt;/xsl:for-each-group&gt;
            &lt;/Categorie&gt;
        &lt;/xsl:for-each-group&gt;
    &lt;/xsl:template&gt;

   &lt;xsl:template match="Row"&gt;
        &lt;Account&gt;
            &lt;xsl:apply-templates/&gt;
        &lt;/Account&gt;
    &lt;/xsl:template&gt;

    &lt;xsl:template match="Row[.//Cell[5]/Data[.='Rating' or .='Gewicht']]"&gt;
        &lt;Header&gt;
            &lt;xsl:apply-templates/&gt;
        &lt;/Header&gt;
    &lt;/xsl:template&gt;

    &lt;xsl:template match="Data"&gt;
        &lt;Data&gt;
            &lt;xsl:value-of select="."/&gt;
        &lt;/Data&gt;
    &lt;/xsl:template&gt;    
&lt;/xsl:stylesheet&gt;
</code></pre>

<p>Outputs:</p>

<pre><code>&lt;Categorie&gt;
   &lt;Account&gt;
      &lt;Data&gt;AAA&lt;/Data&gt;
      &lt;Data&gt;X&lt;/Data&gt;
      &lt;Data&gt;0.01&lt;/Data&gt;
   &lt;/Account&gt;
&lt;/Categorie&gt;
&lt;Categorie&gt;
   &lt;Region&gt;
      &lt;Account&gt;
         &lt;Data&gt;dolor&lt;/Data&gt;
         &lt;Data&gt;123&lt;/Data&gt;
         &lt;Data&gt;A&lt;/Data&gt;
         &lt;Data&gt;0.01&lt;/Data&gt;
      &lt;/Account&gt;
      &lt;Account&gt;
         &lt;Data&gt;sit amet&lt;/Data&gt;
         &lt;Data&gt;445&lt;/Data&gt;
         &lt;Data&gt;B&lt;/Data&gt;
         &lt;Data&gt;0.03&lt;/Data&gt;
      &lt;/Account&gt;
      &lt;Account&gt;
         &lt;Data&gt;consetetur&lt;/Data&gt;
         &lt;Data&gt;36&lt;/Data&gt;
         &lt;Data&gt;B&lt;/Data&gt;
         &lt;Data&gt;8.0000000000000004E-4&lt;/Data&gt;
      &lt;/Account&gt;
   &lt;/Region&gt;
   &lt;Region&gt;
      &lt;Account&gt;
         &lt;Data&gt;sadipscing&lt;/Data&gt;
         &lt;Data&gt;666&lt;/Data&gt;
         &lt;Data&gt;A&lt;/Data&gt;
         &lt;Data&gt;0.01&lt;/Data&gt;
      &lt;/Account&gt;
      &lt;Account&gt;
         &lt;Data&gt;elitr&lt;/Data&gt;
         &lt;Data&gt;97&lt;/Data&gt;
         &lt;Data&gt;C&lt;/Data&gt;
         &lt;Data&gt;0.02&lt;/Data&gt;
      &lt;/Account&gt;
   &lt;/Region&gt;
&lt;/Categorie&gt;
&lt;Categorie&gt;
   &lt;Region&gt;
      &lt;Account&gt;
         &lt;Data&gt;aliquyam&lt;/Data&gt;
         &lt;Data&gt;65&lt;/Data&gt;
         &lt;Data&gt;A&lt;/Data&gt;
         &lt;Data&gt;0.02&lt;/Data&gt;
      &lt;/Account&gt;
      &lt;Account&gt;
         &lt;Data&gt;ipsum&lt;/Data&gt;
         &lt;Data&gt;99&lt;/Data&gt;
         &lt;Data&gt;B&lt;/Data&gt;
         &lt;Data&gt;0.02&lt;/Data&gt;
      &lt;/Account&gt;
   &lt;/Region&gt;
   &lt;Region&gt;
      &lt;Account&gt;
         &lt;Data&gt;lorem&lt;/Data&gt;
         &lt;Data&gt;321&lt;/Data&gt;
         &lt;Data&gt;C&lt;/Data&gt;
         &lt;Data&gt;0.01&lt;/Data&gt;
      &lt;/Account&gt;
   &lt;/Region&gt;
&lt;/Categorie&gt;
</code></pre>

<p><strong>Do note:</strong> your input is missing namespace declarations for <code>x</code> and <code>ss</code> prefix (i.e.  <code>xmlns:x="ns1" xmlns:ss="ns2"</code>). Also, when grouping with starting pattern the matched element is part of the group (thus <code>current-group()[position()&gt;1]</code>) and there might be a first group with all the elements before the first match (thus the <code>xsl:choose</code>). The transformation of <code>Data</code> elements is left out to better understand the main problem.</p>

Q: How can i connect to Apache Cxf web service hosted on Apache Tomcat(Ws security enabled )? A: <p>The solution is the following: update your cxf-beans.xml using:</p>

<pre><code>&lt;cxf:bus&gt;
        &lt;cxf:inInterceptors&gt;
            &lt;ref bean="inIntercTest"/&gt;
        &lt;/cxf:inInterceptors&gt;
        &lt;cxf:outInterceptors&gt;            
            &lt;ref bean="outIntercTest"/&gt;        
        &lt;/cxf:outInterceptors&gt;
    &lt;/cxf:bus&gt;
</code></pre>

<p>instead of:</p>

<pre><code>&lt;cxf:bus&gt;
        &lt;cxf:features&gt;
            &lt;cxf:logging /&gt;
            &lt;wsa:addressing /&gt;
        &lt;/cxf:features&gt;
    &lt;/cxf:bus&gt;
</code></pre>

Q: How to write a single function that allows filtering a collection of objects based on an arbitrary number of passed Types? A: <p>The Jarod42 answer is solid but we can do better. Here are <strong>two improvements</strong> using modern C++ features:</p>
<hr />
<p><strong>Best approach: <code>std::set_intersection</code> + fold expression (C++17)</strong></p>
<p>The SO answer builds a <code>componentIds</code> set and does a per-element <code>count()</code> — O(n log k) — but you can use <code>std::set_intersection</code> which is O(n + k) and more expressive. Even better, skip the intermediate set entirely with a <strong>fold expression</strong>:</p>
<p>Option 1: Variadic + fold (C++17)</p>
<pre><code>// No intermediate set. One-liner predicate via fold-OR.
// Zero-arg case falls through to returning allMyIntegers (see below).

template&lt;typename... Ts&gt;
[[nodiscard]] std::set&lt;int&gt; GetInts(const std::set&lt;int&gt;&amp; allMyIntegers)
{
    if constexpr (sizeof...(Ts) == 0)          // GetInts&lt;&gt;() → all
        return allMyIntegers;

    std::set&lt;int&gt; result;
    for (const int&amp; id : allMyIntegers)
        if ((... || (id == GetComponentId&lt;Ts&gt;()))) // fold-OR over all Ts
            result.insert(id);
    return result;
}
</code></pre>
<p>Option 2: Predicate overload (C++20 concept)</p>
<pre><code>// Accepts any callable — more flexible, composes with lambdas/ranges.
template&lt;std::predicate&lt;int&gt; Pred&gt;
[[nodiscard]] std::set&lt;int&gt; GetInts(const std::set&lt;int&gt;&amp; src, Pred pred)
{
    std::set&lt;int&gt; result;
    std::ranges::copy_if(src, std::inserter(result, result.end()), pred);
    return result;
}
</code></pre>
